{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/955934-spectrum-of-the-dark-rainbow-horror-and-the-chronicles-of-darkness","id":955934,"title":"Spectrum of the Dark Rainbow - Horror and the Chronicles of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-22T15:42:02-07:00","id":955934,"title":"Spectrum of the Dark Rainbow - Horror and the Chronicles of Darkness","content":"I'm terribly sorry for what I figure will probably become an abusive rant, but I just needed to get this off of my chest. As we all know, the Chronicles of Darkness are inherently a horror game. Everything about each and every game line is crafted, from the ground up, to paint a picture of a world steeped in shadow, the supernatural, suffering and sin.<br /> <br /> But... there's many different kinds of horror. More than I have names for, ignorant fool that I am. But the one genre of horror that the Chronicles pride themselves on selling, that its openly stated here to be the fundamental reason behind what makes every single splatline scary, is Personal Horror.<br /> <br /> This is, to my understanding of it, a genre of horror built around introspective and personal decline. It is the horror of spiraling into corruption, madness and malignancy, without even realizing it until it is too late to stop the descent. It is the horror of realizing your beliefs about yourself are false, that you will cast aside your morals if the price is right, and the pain you inflict even on those you care about without stopping.<br /> <br /> Now, let's get this out of the way; this is a very deep and intimate sort of horror. It's a very personalized horror, something that depends, more than any other form of horror, on being tailored to a given individual. It can be truly terrifying, for the kind of person who cares about soul-searching deeply and has the slightest fear about who they are.<br /> <br /> But... is it the <b>right</b> horror to uniformly paint every single gameline in the Chronicles with? Every single Chronicles of Darkness line is supposed to be about Personal Horror, but I just don't think that label fits them all. Vampire, sure, I can buy it there. Even sort of in Changeling, although I think that falls more under the &quot;paranoid horror&quot; label. But in a mortal or hunter game, the horror, to me, is more that of a cosmic horror; it's the horror of realizing that the world is a darker place than you ever realized, and that the civilization you cling to and support is nothing but a veil of lies that struggles to conceal your true place in the world - as prey for creatures far more powerful than you.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest, I first came into the Darkness settings by sheer chance. I stumbled across a battered, secondhand copy of the original edition Clanbook: Nosferatu for Vampire: The Masquerade. I bought it on a whim and I found myself enthralled. I knew absolutely <b>nothing</b> about the greater world that this was part of, but it painted an intricate picture of a world dark, shadowy, and filled with terrible monsters.<br /> <br /> As time went by, my sparse collection of Masquerade books led me to discover the New World of Darkness, after having immersed myself to a very mild degree in the greater metaplots and shenanigans of the Old World. I tried the jump to Requiem, and what I found was in many ways a revelation. Requiem seemed to shake off many of the things that bugged me, like an iron-clad backstory for vampiric origins, the Generations mechanic (how I <b>loathed</b> Generations), and the fact some Clans just seemed fairly monodimensional. There were some problems, mostly a niggling sensation of &quot;tooth pulling&quot; in comparison to Masquerade, but ultimately Requiem was my gateway to the Chronicles and I haven't really looked back since.<br /> <br /> And yet... I can't get past my origins. The Gothick-Punk Dark Urban Fantasy &quot;essence&quot; of the World of Darkness has stained my bones, and I find that, by comparison, even if I love the lore of the Chronicles - the Clans &amp; Bloodlines, Father Wolf and Mother Luna, the Towers of Magic, the Hedge of Thorns, the God-Machine, the Arisen of Du'at - a lot of the actual portrayal of the gamelines just feels... empty.<br /> <br /> I try not to complain about it. Am I not a StoryTeller? Is it not my prerogative to tweak, houserule and homebrew in my own games? If I shuffle the sins of Humanity around under the premise that only the youngest vampires truly wangst over their lost humanity and those who survive more than their first half-century find solace in the Requiem for its own sake, with the Covenants serving vital touchstones to further strengthen a vampire's sanity and hold back the Beast, or if I portray werewolves as having pride in who they are and accepting death in battle as the fitting end for a life of glorious personal freedom, if I say that changelings can learn to embrace their beautiful madness without forsaking their sanity, who am I harming? If I add traces of Gothicism to the architecture and Punk to the street cultures, what offense have I committed against those who prefer a more &quot;rooted in the real world&quot; approach to their game-worlds? if I diminish human importance in the setting and say that monstrosity can be its own valid right, what sin am I committing against those who proudly fly the banners of Humanity Is Special in their own games?<br /> <br /> But, all the same, I seem to have a harder and harder time &quot;getting&quot; the Chronicles of Darkness. Beast, which I thought seemed so promising, ultimately turned out to be just a disappointment - I haven't even been able to muster the conviction to fully read through the corebook yet, I keep getting so far and then I just have to put it down. Promethean was, well, always a bit of a case of Audience Alienating Premise to me, and that feeling still hasn't changed, even though I think that the 2e version, from what little I've had time to read, has made vast improvements towards the kind of Crossover Chronicles I so love. Dark Eras was wonderful, and Demon a delight, but these two... I'm even having a hard time getting too excited about Deviant, just because I get this feeling it's going to borrow and mingle some of the aspects of Beast &amp; Promethean I found most alienating.<br /> <br /> Is there something wrong with me? Everyone on these forums loves the Personal Horror, they shower it with praise and glorify it as the pinnacle of ChroD's design... so why can't I <i>get it</i>? Why do I keep feeling that the gamelines are so much stronger when they embrace a different form of horror and make it their own - that the strength of Mummy is not Personal Horror, but the horror of slavery, despair and futility? That Demon shines so brightly because it discards the tired rote horrors of other settings and instead embraces a heady cocktail of horror, mingling cyber-horror with paranoia with cosmic horror?<br /> <br /> I just... don't understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T15:52:11-07:00","id":955941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/955934-spectrum-of-the-dark-rainbow-horror-and-the-chronicles-of-darkness#post955934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone on these forums loves the Personal Horror, they shower it with praise and glorify it as the pinnacle of ChroD's design...</div> </div> </div> </div>What forums have you been reading, exactly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T15:56:32-07:00","id":955945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/955934-spectrum-of-the-dark-rainbow-horror-and-the-chronicles-of-darkness#post955934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there something wrong with me?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Everyone on these forums loves the Personal Horror, they shower it with praise and glorify it as the pinnacle of ChroD's design... </div> </div> </div>That's untrue. Many people complain about personal horror all the time, some post in threads bout personal horror just to go on and on about how they don't see any horror in it, and many throw off the horror to just play urban fantasy games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why do I keep feeling that the gamelines are so much stronger when they embrace a different form of horror and make it their own - that the strength of Mummy is not Personal Horror, but the horror of slavery, despair and futility? That Demon shines so brightly because it discards the tired rote horrors of other settings and instead embraces a heady cocktail of horror, mingling cyber-horror with paranoia with cosmic horror? </div> </div> </div>Having read your post I really think you're placing too much of an emphasis on personal horror. It doesn't have to be the only aspect of horror in the game, or even one that is above all others. The concept doesn't even come up in Werewolf the Forsaken's second edition, which mentions savage horror and body horror numerous times. Part of Demon's horror, said so by the book, is the drive towards becoming something else and not knowing or having control of what one is becoming. There's no reason you have to take themes of horror you see and enjoy and throw them away to just play personal horror, and I'm sure none of the books demand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T15:56:57-07:00","id":955946,"title":"","content":"I personally run CofD as more urban fantasy with a dash pf horror myself. The thing is, the CofD is a toolbox, different groups run it different ways and they are all CofD.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't see Beast or Promethean as personal horror. I see Beast as &quot;I like being a monster, so fuck angst and help me set up this death trap for that annoying hero!&quot; and Promethean as being about hope for a better tomorrow and the struggle to constantly improve yourself when the world is telling you to give up. It's the same with all the game lines, they can be thematically interpenetrated different ways by different groups and that is part of the toolbox nature of it.<br /> <br /> So, nothing is wrong with you, it's just that the people who interpret it as personal horror and only that can be a little loud sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T17:35:18-07:00","id":956015,"title":"","content":"Depends on what you mean by &quot;personal horror.&quot; The CofD games go way beyond the personal horror genre pioneered by <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i>. But they're all games with personal stakes and horrific themes.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Perhaps more to the point, do what you want with the games. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> We produce fairly focused games, but they're meant to be modified and adapted to you and your friends' needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 08-22-2016, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T18:01:30-07:00","id":956036,"title":"","content":"You're not gonna like every single gameline. I know I don't.<br /> <br /> But I do take some small umbrage at the assertion that Hunter isn't personal horror. When last week, you were a middle school math teacher with no knowledge of the supernatural, and how you're dousing a vampire tied to a chair with gasoline and setting him ablaze because, y'know, he's a /monster/... that's an incredibly intimate form of horror, to say nothing of the Conspiracies who dabble in &quot;oh my god, I have the blood of the Adversary in my veins&quot; or &quot;oh my god, I have an alien parasite implanted in my spine.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T00:47:08-07:00","id":956195,"title":"","content":"To be frank, I think that each<b> CoD</b> game has it\u2019s own flavor of horror. Yeah, in most fundamental level, most ( but not even all ) have some string in Personal Horror because of Integrity mechanics, but as all \u2013 each game gives you it\u2019s own horror experience. And it\u2019s WHY they are different games in the first place. Here is base sum up:<ul><li><b>Vampire: The Requiem</b> \u2013 Classical Personal Horror of \u2018what monster I become\u2019</li> <li><b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b> \u2013 Savage Horror of true brutality and \u2018I will hunt <i>you</i>\u2019</li> <li><b>Mage: The Awakening </b>\u2013 Alternative Personal Horror of consequence and \u2018what can you do with power\u2019</li> <li><b>Promethean: The Created</b> \u2013 Horror of being \u2018Other\u2019 with a large dosage of nihilism \u2018looking for humanity is pointless\u2019</li> <li><b>Changeling: The Lost</b> \u2013 Horror of \u2018never look back or they <i>will</i> find you\u2019</li> <li><b>Hunter: The Vigil</b> \u2013 Twist on Personal Horror of \u2018Fighting with monster watch out to become one\u2019</li> <li><b>Geist: The Sin-Eaters</b> \u2013 Horror of \u2018dead don\u2019t forget\u2019</li> <li><b>Mummy: The Curse </b>\u2013 Horror of how much you forgot ( I suspect here, did not read more than few spoilers of game )</li> <li><b>Demon: The Descent </b>\u2013 Paranoid Horror of \u2018God Machine can be <i>everywhere</i>\u2019</li> <li><b>Beast: The Primordial</b> \u2013 Horror of \u2018I\u2019m monster and I NEED to feed\u2019 \u2013 It can be said as variant on Personal Horror of <b>Vampire</b>.</li> <li><b>Deviant: The Renegades </b>\u2013 Probably it will be a mix of <b>Demon</b> and <b>Beast</b> horrors in a way \u2018What have they made me into?!\u2019</li> </ul>Nominally <b>Werewolf</b>, <b>Promethean</b> and <b>Beast</b> have the least connection with Personal Horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-23-2016, 03:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T02:14:20-07:00","id":956218,"title":"","content":"I find there's plenty of personal horror on werewolf. My main source of fear in that game is knowing that you are always a bad moment away to wake up covered in the guts of your loved ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T09:02:27-07:00","id":956349,"title":"","content":"All of the game lines <i>can</i> be played as personal horror, and I run them that way because I love personal horror. But they don't have to be run that way if you're not into it, and there's certainly nothing wrong with that. Also, personal horror, external horror, urban fantasy, these things don't have to be mutually exclusive. Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage all have elements of all three in my opinion. And don't sweat not liking all the game lines. They're very focused, so it's totally understandable if there are a few you don't care for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}